WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
I've been a mechanic for 20 years and I still
see mechanics wasting their time and money

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.400
with these three work lights.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.560
Number one, the standard flashlight.

4
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.000
Every mechanic starts here.

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.760
It's reliable, it's simple, and it's cheap.

6
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.000
The problem is that it can only point in one
direction.

7
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.880
So when you're working on a job that isn't
directly in front of you, the light hits

8
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:24.680
whatever is in the way first and the thing you
actually need to see is in the shadows.

9
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.760
It also forces you to work with one hand, or
you got to hold it in your mouth,

10
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.200
it just isn't ideal.

11
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.960
Number two, the under hood bar.

12
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.720
You clip it to the hood, it floods the whole
engine bay

13
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.800
and it genuinely feels like you finally solve
the problem

14
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.740
until you need to get inside a wheel arch,

15
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.680
work under the dash or do anything

16
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.240
that isn't sitting right on top of the engine.

17
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.880
The bar is mounted at the hood line

18
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.200
and shines straight down onto the surface.

19
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.720
The deeper you go into the car,

20
00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:50.960
the less light you have

21
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.440
and then you're back to squinting and
guessing.

22
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.000
And the moment you close the hood

23
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.780
or move to a different part of the car,

24
00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.120
it's completely useless.

25
00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.440
You've spent good money on a light that only
works

26
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.120
in one position, on one part of the car.

27
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.960
Number three, the headlamp.

28
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.120
This is what guys switch to when they want
both hands free.

29
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.840
And I understand why, it works in theory.

30
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.900
But the light goes where your head goes,

31
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.180
not where your hands are.

32
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.960
When you're reaching into a tight space,

33
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.400
your hands are pointing one way

34
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.880
and your head is pointing another.

35
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.240
And even when you get your head in the perfect
position,

36
00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.960
your own hands are casting a shadow

37
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.040
directly over what you're trying to see

38
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.140
because the light is coming from behind you.

39
00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.900
you're constantly adjusting your head

40
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.540
just to keep the light on the job

41
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.180
instead of having 100% focus on the work.

42
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.380
So what do I recommend?

43
00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.940
This is what I use, the Antiklo Flexi Light.

44
00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.860
It's a flexible LED light

45
00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.180
that I can put directly into where I need
light

46
00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.980
and it illuminates everything around it.

47
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.580
So you're no longer pointing a light

48
00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.740
at the problem from the outside anymore.

49
00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.740
The light is literally right in the area which
you need it.

50
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.100
It also means you can have both hands on the
job,

51
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.500
giving you full focus

52
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.360
and saving you from a lot of frustration

53
00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.100
that just isn't necessary.

54
00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.820
it works perfectly with engine bays.

55
00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.220
You can wrap it in wheel wells,

56
00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.780
use it for under-dash electric work, et
cetera.

57
00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:04.660
You don't have to worry about replacing
batteries

58
00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.820
because it's rechargeable,

59
00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.060
and it lasts seven hours on a full charge

60
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.900
so it easily gets you through the day.

61
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.460
This is by far the best light

62
00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.980
in terms of versatility, efficiency,

63
00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.220
and bang for your buck.

64
00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.220
You can get them at the link below.
